# Source of Truth: pub

Summary: The scoped authority map for this project. Each subject has exactly one declared authority; locations must be real paths or references, or marked `unresolved`/`not applicable`. Never list hypothetical paths and never keep two active authorities for one scope.

| Subject/scope | Authority | Location | State or revision |
|---|---|---|---|
| Observable behavior (current) | OpenSpec (detected; confirm authority) | `pub/openspec/specs/` | <discover: revision or date> |
| Observable behavior (proposed) | OpenSpec (detected; confirm authority) | `pub/openspec/changes/` | <discover: revision or date> |
| API contract | <discover: authority or not applicable> | <discover: actual path or not applicable> | <discover: revision or date> |
| Database/schema | <discover: authority or not applicable> | <discover: actual path or not applicable> | <discover: revision or date> |
| Configuration keys/defaults | <discover: authority or not applicable> | <discover: actual path or not applicable> | <discover: revision or date> |
| Go dependencies | pub repository | `pub/go.mod` | `pub/go.sum` |
| Python dependencies | <discover: `pub` repository or not applicable> | <discover: `pub/pyproject.toml` or not applicable> | <discover: `pub/uv.lock` or not applicable> |
| Cargo dependencies | <discover: `pub` repository or not applicable> | <discover: `pub/Cargo.toml` or not applicable> | <discover: `pub/Cargo.lock` or not applicable> |
| Go integration overlay | private meta-repository | `/go.work` | <discover: revision or date> |
| Python integration overlay | private meta-repository | <discover: `/pyproject.toml` + `/uv.lock` or not applicable> | <discover: revision or date> |
| Cargo integration overlay | private meta-repository | <discover: `/Cargo.toml` or not applicable> | <discover: revision or date> |
| Build/release implementation | pub repository | <discover: Makefile/script/CI path> | <discover: revision or date> |
| Technical decisions | this project's private context | `.agents/context/pub/decisions/` | accepted ADRs |
| Execution status | this project's private context | `.agents/context/pub/status.md` | informational only |

Authority is scoped: different subjects may have different authoritative sources without duplication. A draft issue or agent suggestion does not override an accepted requirement; implementation is evidence of actual behavior, and a discrepancy with the agreed requirement is reported, not silently normalized. An external authority remains authoritative even when it cannot be fetched; record the gap instead of fabricating its contents.
